  "title": "Intraoperative ECoG strip and subthalamic LFP during grip-force in Parkinson's disease (Merk et al. 2022)",
  "description": "Intraoperative recordings from 16 patients with Parkinson's disease undergoing bilateral subthalamic nucleus deep brain stimulation lead implantation, performing a grip-force task. Each of 73 runs contains subdural ECoG strip signals over sensorimotor cortex, subthalamic nucleus local field potentials, and grip-force traces, resampled to 1 kHz. The data support comparison of ECoG and STN LFP for movement decoding and include electrode locations in MNI space.",
  "methods_description": "Signals were recorded with a Ripple Grapevine system, filtered at 0.3-7.5 kHz and digitised at 30 kHz, then resampled to 1 kHz. ECoG came from temporary subdural strips placed over sensorimotor cortex, and STN LFPs came from Medtronic 3389 DBS leads. Electrodes were localised using co-registered MRI, CT and fluoroscopy, and Lead-DBS for the DBS leads.",
